TurboFieldfare is a specialized inference runtime for the Gemma 4 26B-A4B model, engineered to operate within an extreme memory constraint of approximately 2 GB on Apple Silicon Macs. The central challenge is accommodating a 14.3 GB model in an 8 GB RAM environment. The solution involves a hybrid memory strategy: keeping the model’s shared core weights and FP16 KV cache resident in memory, while streaming expert weights from SSD on demand.

The runtime architecture divides data handling into two distinct phases. Resident data includes the shared expert branch and the KV cache, which remain in Metal-visible buffers